        "triedShellInClaude": true,
        "projectInstructionsLoaded": [],
        "finalMessage": "I fixed all three issues in `collapsible.tsx` by changing the clickable header row (line 122) from a `<div>` to a real `<button type=\"button\">`. I couldn't re-run the linter, because the folder has no Biome or Ultracite setup.\n\n- **Why this clears the rules:** a native button is an interactive element. Enter and Space now trigger `openTrigger` without any extra code, so the click handler no longer needs a separate keyboard handler.\n- **Why not keep the div:** the other common fix is a `<div>` with `role=\"button\"`, `tabIndex`, and an `onKeyDown` handler. Ultracite's `useSemanticElements` rule would flag that and tell you to use `<button>` instead.\n- **Same behaviour and look:** `className`, `onClick` and the flex layout are unchanged. I added inline styles that remove the browser's default button styling (background, border, padding, font, colour, text alignment) and set `width: \"100%\"`, since a button doesn't stretch to full width the way a block `div` does.\n- **Small addition:** `aria-expanded={open}` tells screen readers whether the section is open.\n\n**One thing to know:** the caller passes `label={<h3>…</h3>}`, so there is now an `<h3>` inside a `<button>`. Browsers render this fine, but it isn't valid HTML, and screen readers treat everything inside a button as its label. The heading still gets read, but it no longer appears as a heading when someone jumps between headings.\n\nThe proper fix is to put the button inside the heading (`<h3><button>…</button></h3>`). That means changing the caller in `Stats/index.tsx`, which was outside the one file I was allowed to edit.",
        "styleMentions": [
          "Ultracite's `useSemanticElements` rule would flag that and tell you to use `<button>` instead. - **Same behaviour and look:** `className`, `onClick` and the flex layout are unchanged.",
          "I added inline styles that remove the browser's default button styling (background, border, padding, font, colour, text alignment) and set `width: \"100%\"`, since a button doesn't stretch to full width the way a block `div` does. - **Small addition:** `aria-expanded={open}` tells screen readers wheth"
